 ```
 
+The dispatch e2e test (`app/api/runtime/dispatch.e2e.test.ts`) spawns a
+fake `claude` binary on disk; the runner asks for cwd `/workspace` (the
+path inside a real VM), so the test's driver falls back to the fixture
+directory when that path does not exist on the host. Its wait for
+`run.finished` over SSE is bounded by `SWARM_DISPATCH_E2E_TIMEOUT_MS`
+(default `30000`): a run that stalls fails with the events seen so far
+instead of hanging the suite. The same ordering invariants are also covered
+without any child process by `app/api/runtime/dispatch.test.ts`, which
+replays the recorded transcript through the in-memory `FakeVmDriver`.
+
 Run the whole gate in one command (typecheck → unit → build → boot the built
 app on a free port with `SWARM_VM_DRIVER=fake` and a temp `SWARM_HOME` → local
 e2e → shutdown; exits non-zero on the first failure). Requires the Playwright
